1
00:00:04,220 --> 00:00:05,960
麦克斯 邮差先生来[射]了
Max, look, the mailman came.

2
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:07,721
到哪边 你胸上 还是头发上
Where am I looking, your chest, your hair?

3
00:00:07,721 --> 00:00:09,315
给个提示嘛
Gimme a hint.

4
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:14,760
是这个啦 我们的驱逐令
It's here. Our eviction notice.

5
00:00:14,940 --> 00:00:15,780
只需4毛6
It's amazing you can send

6
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:17,800
就能把天大耻辱送到你手 真了不起
this much shame for just 46 cents.

7
00:00:18,940 --> 00:00:21,000
不是吧 半年才少交三个月租金就得走啊
What, you miss three out of six months and you're out?

8
00:00:21,440 --> 00:00:22,560
打击命中率高达5成呢[棒球]
We're batting 500.

9
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:24,280
我们应该进名人堂的 好吗
That's hall of fame stuff right there.

10
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:25,840
姑娘们
Hi, girls.

11
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:27,840
我就顺路过来买个小蛋糕
I just stopped by to get a cupcake

12
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:29,220
在去健身房的路上吃
to eat on the way to the gym.

13
00:00:31,180 --> 00:00:32,340
好 你先坐一下
Here, have a seat.

14
00:00:32,360 --> 00:00:33,320
我去拿你喜欢的口味
I'll get you your usual.

15
00:00:34,360 --> 00:00:35,816
麦克斯 柠檬蛋白霜小蛋糕呢
Max, where are the lemon meringue cupcakes?

16
00:00:35,816 --> 00:00:37,180
不做了
Stopped making 'em.

17
00:00:37,180 --> 00:00:38,320
浆果软糖味
And the fudge berries

18
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:39,040
和紫丝绒蛋糕也不做了
And the purple velvets.

19
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:41,300
我们每天都剩超多
We have so many left over every day

20
00:00:41,300 --> 00:00:43,361
就连我每晚送小蛋糕给她的流浪妇女都说
that even the homeless lady I give them to at night

21
00:00:43,361 --> 00:00:46,107
"小女孩 你的小店要倒了 是吧"
was like, "girl, your shop in trouble, ain't it?"

22
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:47,900
所以呢 麦克斯
So what, Max?

23
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:49,460
我们应该听从一个认为
You think we should take business advice

24
00:00:49,460 --> 00:00:51,520
我国应该用麦乐鸡来当货币的
from a woman who thinks our nation's currency

25
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:52,500
流浪妇女的商业建议吗
should be the McNugget?

26
00:00:54,240 --> 00:00:55,840
人家言之有理啊
She makes a good point.

27
00:00:58,180 --> 00:01:01,340
现在气氛好像有点太剑拔弩张了
I think it's getting a little too real in here for me.

28
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:04,680
我要去托高我的胸 顺便粘粘我的假牙
I'm gonna go push up my boobs and glue my tooth back on.

29
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:09,240
说真的 这事我们怎么处理
Seriously, what are we gonna do about this?

30
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:10,500
我来教你怎么做吧
I'll tell you what we're gonna do.

31
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:14,660
你撕烂了一封驱逐信
Aww, you ripped up an eviction notice.

32
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:17,700
这是以前我会跟我妈妈一起做的事呢
That's the one thing my mother and I used to do together.

33
00:01:32,740 --> 00:01:34,700
麦克斯 我知道咱们店情况不乐观
Max, I know our shop's in trouble.

34
00:01:34,780 --> 00:01:35,900
我也整天在想这问题
It's all I think about.

35
00:01:36,020 --> 00:01:37,400
连我在做的春梦
Even in my sexual fantasies,

36
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:39,180
都是我在付房租给瑞恩·高斯林[帅哥男星]
I'm giving Ryan Gosling a rent check.

37
00:01:41,140 --> 00:01:44,100
我只希望上天给个指示 指点我们方向
I just wish we had a sign that told us what to do.

38
00:01:45,620 --> 00:01:46,500
你看 来客人了
See? Customers.

39
00:01:46,500 --> 00:01:47,840
预示着我们的店不会倒
That's a sign to stay open.

40
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:49,120
给 赶紧装忙
Here, pretend to be busy.

41
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:51,320
我们会立刻给你送过去
We'll send those right out.

42
00:01:51,440 --> 00:01:52,600
谢谢你的致电 奥普拉[知名女主持]
Thank you for calling, Oprah.

43
00:01:56,300 --> 00:01:57,900
你好 我是乔安·莫尔斯
Hi, I'm Joanne Morse.

44
00:01:58,160 --> 00:02:00,600
真希望我也能有钱到有人替我开口说话
I wish I was rich enough to have somebody talk for me.

45
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:03,580
麦克斯 你瞎啊 她是聋的
Max, are you blind? She's deaf.

46
00:02:05,260 --> 00:02:06,120
好酷哦
So cool.

47
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:08,140
自从她搬进来后 我就很希望变聋子
I've wanted to be deaf ever since she moved in.

48
00:02:09,460 --> 00:02:12,520
我是田纳商业地产公司的代表
I'm a representative from Tenner Commercial Real Estate.

49
00:02:12,940 --> 00:02:14,200
我们想要得到您这单位
We're acquiring this property

50
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:15,600
我们愿意出钱收购你的店面
and would like to offer you a corporate buy out.

51
00:02:16,460 --> 00:02:18,500
完全不懂 她说的我还比较懂呢
I understood that better when she said it.

52
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:24,040
谢谢您的邀请 但我们没有兴趣
Thank you very much, but we're not interested.

53
00:02:24,440 --> 00:02:25,740
我也会一点手语
I speak a little sign language.

54
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:27,900
你刚才说的是"非常谢谢
You just said "Thank you very much,

55
00:02:27,900 --> 00:02:29,100
但我现在没有穿内衣哦"
but I'm not wearing underwear."

56
00:02:31,880 --> 00:02:34,100
我就知道以前的手语家教在玩我
I knew that tutor was screwing with me.

57
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:36,540
而且没穿内衣那个是我啦
And I'm the one not wearing underwear.

58
00:02:39,960 --> 00:02:43,820
我们愿意出两万五的价格买下你的租约
We're ready to offer you $25,000 to take over your lease.

59
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:44,940
他奶奶的 当然好啊
Hell yes, bitch.

60
00:02:46,280 --> 00:02:47,820
麦克斯 不行 你别乱说话
Max, no. What are you doing?

61
00:02:47,920 --> 00:02:49,140
这小店是我们的梦想
This shop is our dream.

62
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:51,760
我们这梦想都快成恶梦了
Well, our dream is turning into a nightmare

63
00:02:51,760 --> 00:02:53,560
而且没人会来唤醒我们
and no one's coming to wake us up.

64
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:55,700
这是我们的未来
This is our future.

65
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:58,680
抱歉了 真的很谢谢您 但我们不会卖的
I'm sorry, thank you very much, but we're gonna pass.

66
00:02:58,780 --> 00:02:59,880
我们的生意刚开始蒸蒸日上
Our business is booming.

67
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:03,640
哎哟
Oh, yeah.

68
00:03:03,820 --> 00:03:05,600
看这小伙
Look at him.

69
00:03:07,220 --> 00:03:08,900
"来吧 时尚"
Come on and Vogue.

70
00:03:09,860 --> 00:03:10,620
没错
Yes.

71
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,300
跟着音乐跳吧
Yeah, dance to the music.

72
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:19,580
还记得麦当娜还在世的那会吗
Remember when Madonna was alive?

73
00:03:21,820 --> 00:03:24,140
那些年可真是美好岁月啊
Those were the good old days.

74
00:03:25,140 --> 00:03:27,400
我们会给你们一点时间考虑
We'll give you some time to think about it,

75
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:29,140
不过你们拖欠租金次数过多
but with your delinquent rent history,

76
00:03:29,340 --> 00:03:32,460
就算你们想留下 也得先预交六个月的租金
if you stay, we would need six months' rent up front.

77
00:03:32,560 --> 00:03:35,160
我建议你们收下这两万五吧
So I'd take the $25,000.

78
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:36,480
这条件很不错了
It's a good deal.

79
00:03:41,300 --> 00:03:46,860
我们会打给你 好吗
Uh, uh, we...call...you. Okay?

80
00:03:54,180 --> 00:03:56,100
苏菲 这又不关你的事
Sophie, it's none of your business.

81
00:03:56,180 --> 00:03:57,520
这事得我们自己决定
This is our decision.

82
00:03:58,620 --> 00:04:00,880
你自己说想要上天给个指示的啊
You said you were looking for a sign.

83
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:03,720
指手划脚的手语不就是最明显的指示了吗
What's more of a sign than sign language?

84
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:06,800
不行 不必多说了
No. End of story.

85
00:04:06,840 --> 00:04:08,260
就算给我全世界的"麦乐鸡"
I would not sell this shop

86
00:04:08,260 --> 00:04:10,120
我也不会卖掉这小店
for all the McNuggets in the world.

87
00:04:10,720 --> 00:04:12,320
我对我们的梦想还有信心
I still believe in our dream,

88
00:04:12,320 --> 00:04:13,640
这梦想也绝不该在聋子中介
and it does not end with an offer

89
00:04:13,640 --> 00:04:15,220
随便开个价后就轻易结束
from the deaf real estate jam.

90
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:19,980
女人啊 就爱意气用事
Women. Am I right?

91
00:04:24,480 --> 00:04:25,880
厄尔 有事想你给点指教
Earl, I need some advice.

92
00:04:26,260 --> 00:04:27,620
有人向我跟卡洛琳开价
Caroline and I were offered money

93
00:04:27,620 --> 00:04:28,900
想收购我们小店的店面
to buy out the cupcake store,

94
00:04:29,060 --> 00:04:31,440
我的守护神 "肯尼·罗杰斯"曾问过
and as my spirit animal, Kenny Rogers, once asked,

95
00:04:33,060 --> 00:04:34,640
"何时该叫牌 而何时该盖牌呢"
"When do you hold 'em and when do you fold 'em?"

96
00:04:37,280 --> 00:04:39,440
麦克斯 人生中有两样东西
Well, Max, there are two things in life

97
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:40,960
你必需得留下
you've got to hold on to:

98
00:04:41,180 --> 00:04:44,680
"你的梦想" 以及在商店买完东西后的发票
your dreams, and your receipt when you're leaving Best Buy.

99
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:50,100
没发票的黑人绝对是茅房里提灯笼 找屎[死]啊
Oh, you do not want to be a black man without a receipt.

100
00:04:55,340 --> 00:04:57,040
麦克斯 你是在故意不甩我吗
Max, did you just give me the cold shoulder?

101
00:04:57,220 --> 00:04:59,140
天啊 我试着故意不甩你一年半了
Oh, my God, I've been doing that for a year and a half

102
00:04:59,140 --> 00:05:00,260
你今天终于明白了
and you finally got it.

103
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:03,560
今天那么甩头就走是我不对
I'm sorry for storming out earlier,

104
00:05:03,560 --> 00:05:05,420
但我们不能这么轻易放弃
but we just can't give it up that easy.

105
00:05:05,940 --> 00:05:07,820
我能 也有过 也会继续这么做
I can, and have, and will again.

106
00:05:10,320 --> 00:05:12,240
我们现在抽身 说不定是明智之举呢
Maybe it's better if we just get out now.

107
00:05:12,300 --> 00:05:13,500
我听到一个顾客在说
I heard a customer saying

108
00:05:13,500 --> 00:05:15,200
全食超市要在附近开新店面呢
a Whole Foods is going in over there.

109
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:16,680
你知道什么人会去那里买东西吗
You know who goes to Whole Foods?

110
00:05:16,940 --> 00:05:19,120
穿着怪胎五指鞋的有钱妇女
Rich ladies with those freaky toe sneakers.

111
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:24,480
老娘绝对不想看见穿怪胎五指鞋的人
And I cannot be seeing no freaky toe sneakers.

112
00:05:26,060 --> 00:05:26,740
全食超市吗
Whole Foods?

113
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:29,280
这就是我想看到的老天爷指示啊
That's the sign I've been looking for.

114
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:30,800
难怪他们想赶我们走呢
No wonder they wanted to get rid of us.

115
00:05:30,820 --> 00:05:31,660
全食超市一开
With a whole foods there,

116
00:05:31,660 --> 00:05:33,060
他们就能合理涨租金
they can raise everybody's rent.

117
00:05:33,280 --> 00:05:34,760
没差啊 反正我们又不付
That's fine, we don't pay it anyway.

118
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:38,900
我就知道这里会成为炙手可热的新区
I knew it was gonna be the hot new neighborhood.

119
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:40,460
被我料中了 能行了 麦克斯
I knew it! This is it, Max.

120
00:05:40,520 --> 00:05:42,500
全食超市一进驻 基佬们就会跟着来
First comes the Whole Foods, then come the gays,

121
00:05:42,540 --> 00:05:43,380
然后明星也会过来
then the celebrities.

122
00:05:43,380 --> 00:05:44,820
我们附近有公园
Well, the gays will come anyway

123
00:05:44,820 --> 00:05:45,940
本来就能吸引一大堆基佬
as long as there's a park.

124
00:05:48,460 --> 00:05:50,400
麦克斯 说真的 成功只是早晚的问题
Seriously, Max, it's just a matter of time

125
00:05:50,400 --> 00:05:51,800
我们很快就有机会对安妮·海瑟薇说
before we're telling Anne Hathaway,

126
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:53,020
"你的假笑不管用
"Forget that fake smile

127
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:54,660
想买小蛋糕就跟大家一样乖乖排队"
and just go wait in line like everybody else."

128
00:05:55,890 --> 00:05:57,800
阿憨 我们小蛋糕店附近
Han, they're opening up a whole Foods

129
00:05:57,800 --> 00:05:59,160
要开一家全食超市呢
right near our cupcake shop.

130
00:05:59,460 --> 00:06:00,600
又一家全食超市啊
Another Whole Foods?

131
00:06:00,780 --> 00:06:03,560
是不是要等"全食"变"全国"他们才满意啊
They won't be happy till it's "Whole Country," am I right?

132
00:06:05,260 --> 00:06:06,740
我在网上个帖子里看到的
I saw that on a meme.

133
00:06:08,460 --> 00:06:10,420
当务之急是要守住这家宝店
Now we have to stay in that neighborhood.

134
00:06:10,520 --> 00:06:13,040
我们只要想出去哪筹六个月的租金就行了
We just have to come up with six months rent up front.

135
00:06:13,740 --> 00:06:15,100
女孩们 我很乐意伸出援手
Well, I'd love to help you, ladies,

136
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:17,440
但我在2008年 就忘了我银行卡的密码
but I forgot my pin number in 2008.

137
00:06:19,140 --> 00:06:20,640
等等 2008
Wait a minute, 2008.

138
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:21,980
那就是我的密码
That's my pin number!

139
00:06:29,420 --> 00:06:30,896
你们想跟我借啊
You want my money?

140
00:06:30,896 --> 00:06:33,056
偶的天啊
Ehr mah gerd.

141
00:06:34,160 --> 00:06:35,840
我最近在网上看了很多热帖
I've been looking at a lot of memes.

142
00:06:36,880 --> 00:06:38,760
我想起来你长得像谁了
Oh, that's who you look like.

143
00:06:38,800 --> 00:06:39,760
暴躁猫
Grumpy cat!

144
00:06:43,040 --> 00:06:45,620
麦克斯 我知道我们能借的都借了
Max, I know we've borrowed from everyone we know,

145
00:06:45,620 --> 00:06:47,800
但我非常确定这条路是对的
but I'm so convinced that this is the right thing

146
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:50,160
我愿意牺牲去做一件
that I'm willing to stoop to something

147
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:52,160
我永远也不会做的事
I never thought I'd do.

148
00:06:52,460 --> 00:06:54,560
你的确是很甜美又可爱
Look, you're sweet and you're adorable,

149
00:06:54,620 --> 00:06:56,820
但是你太骨感了 一个晚上顶多只能"赚"到40
but you're way too bony to bring in more than 40 a night.

150
00:06:59,260 --> 00:07:01,380
就算你有只动物做噱头搭档
And even if you got an animal sidekick,

151
00:07:01,380 --> 00:07:02,700
我们还是到不了那目标
it's still not gonna get us there.

152
00:07:04,240 --> 00:07:05,680
但是够我"到"了
It would get me there.

153
00:07:07,860 --> 00:07:10,160
我们可以预约一下 去市中心
We can make an appointment, go into the city,

154
00:07:10,160 --> 00:07:11,700
然后跟我查莉蒂姑姑借钱
and ask my Aunt Charity for the money.

155
00:07:11,700 --> 00:07:13,480
她是化妆品王国的总裁
She's president of a cosmetic empire

156
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:14,840
富得流油
and she's filthy rich.

157
00:07:15,160 --> 00:07:17,920
那为什么你什么屁话都说
And how is she literally the only thing

158
00:07:17,920 --> 00:07:18,940
却从没提起过她啊
you've never talked about?

159
00:07:20,460 --> 00:07:22,040
因为她很讨厌我啊
Because she hates me.

160
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:24,020
亲人就是这样啊
That's what family is.

161
00:07:24,440 --> 00:07:26,585
亲人就是恨你 但又不能杀你的人
People who hate you, but can't kill you

162
00:07:26,585 --> 00:07:28,217
因为你死了 警察会第一个找他们问话
'cause they're the first ones questioned.

163
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:36,720
真没想到你们还在等
I'm surprised you're still waiting.

164
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:38,920
大多数人等两个小时就走人了
Most people leave after two hours.

165
00:07:39,960 --> 00:07:41,760
没事 我们能等
Well, it's not a problem for us.

166
00:07:41,860 --> 00:07:43,940
要我们等两小时 三小时 一天都没问题
We'll wait two hours, three, a whole day.

167
00:07:44,080 --> 00:07:45,420
等一天估计差不多了
That sounds about right.

168
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:49,500
-斯蒂芬妮 -来了
- Stephanie. - Coming.

169
00:07:51,080 --> 00:07:52,460
我不叫这名字
That's not my name,

170
00:07:53,380 --> 00:07:54,900
但是我不敢纠正她
but I'm afraid to tell her.

